<title>ISRAEL: Tel Aviv bourse to replace two Maof index shares.</title>
<headline>Tel Aviv bourse to replace two Maof index shares.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tel Aviv Stock Exchange's board of directors will vote on July 10 on a proposal to make changes to the Maof 25 blue chip index, the bourse said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Under the proposal, Leumi Insurance and Clal Insurance would be added to the Maof while Africa Israel Investments and Israel Corp would be removed.</p>
<p>The changes would take effect on August 3.</p>
<p>The index, comprised of the shares with the biggest market value, will be updated every February and August, the bourse said.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-2-537-0502 TCC</p>
</text>
